## 2. Measures of Forecast Accuracy

To evaluate how well a time series model performs, we use standard quantitative metrics comparing predicted values ($\hat{y}_t$) against actual values ($y_t$):

| Metric | Formula / Description | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **MAE** (Mean Absolute Error) | $\frac{1}{n} \sum |y_t - \hat{y}_t|$ | Measures average magnitude of errors in absolute terms. |
| **MSE** (Mean Squared Error) | $\frac{1}{n} \sum (y_t - \hat{y}_t)^2$ | Penalizes larger errors heavily by squaring them. |
| **RMSE** (Root Mean Squared Error) | $\sqrt{\text{MSE}}$ | Expressed in the same units as the original data. |
| **MAPE** (Mean Absolute Percentage Error) | $\frac{100\%}{n} \sum \left|\frac{y_t - \hat{y}_t}{y_t}\right|$ | Expresses accuracy as a percentage for easy interpretation. |

